Here are a few examples of `for` loops in different programming languages. Choose the one you need:

### Python

```python
for i in range(1, 11):
    print(i)
```

This prints numbers 1 through 10.

---

### JavaScript

```javascript
for (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    console.log(i);
}
```

Prints numbers 1 through 10 in the browser console.

---

### Java

```java
for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    System.out.println(i);
}
```

Prints numbers 1 through 10 in the console.

---

### C

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
        printf("%d\n", i);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Prints numbers 1 through 10.

---

### C++

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
        cout << i << endl;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Prints numbers 1 through 10.

